ED_RE`**: the module constant, after `MAX_AGE_SECONDS`, with the exact pattern and `re.IGNORECASE`.\n- **`_purge_not_constructed(conn)`**: selects the `Tournaments/Topdeck/%` events, picks out those whose name matches, and deletes them with their rows. Twins pointing at a purged event have `duplicate_of` cleared. I ran all the matching deletions in one transaction, not one per event. The spec's wording allowed either, and one transaction means a failure leaves nothing half-purged. It logs one warning with the count, and does nothing when nothing matches.\n- **`refresh_topdeck`**: skips a tournament whose name matches, with a warning and a `skipped` increment, after the existing no-TID check. It calls `_purge_not_constructed(conn)` right after `store_events`.\n\nI did not run the full test suite or the dashboard checks, since the spec's list only named these two commands and this change is confined to the metagame module. `SPEC.md` was already untracked before I started, and I left it alone.", "ttft_ms": 1609, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 37069, "uuid": "6b1739d8-c311-4d97-bf09-1b7adf8eec58", "ttft_stream_ms": 1444, "time_to_request_ms": 511, "first_content_frame_ms": 1444, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
